<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sophia of Hanover</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1630–<a href="/years/1714">1714</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sophia of the Palatinate, Electress Sophia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sophia of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> was a princess of the Palatinate, daughter of Frederick V and Elizabeth Stuart, who married Ernest Augustus, later Elector of Hanover. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> of 1701 named her and her Protestant descendants heirs to the English throne. She died weeks before Queen Anne, so her son became King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-i-of-great-britain">George I of Great Britain</a> in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sophia-of-hanover.jpg" alt="Sophia of Hanover" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerard van Honthorst · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerrit_van_Honthorst_(c.1590-1592-1656)_-_Electress_Sophia_(1630%E2%80%931714),_Princess_Palatine,_Consort_of_Ernest_Augustus,_Elector_of_Hanover_-_493063_-_National_Trust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
